    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328-a3">

                <pb facs="0767" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg671"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-07-09"><hi rendition="#small-caps">July</hi> 9,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In my note of the 3d instant I informed you
                    that in connection with the prevalence of cholera in the localities of Kobe and
                    Ozaka, vessels arriving from those localities would be detained during ten days
                    at Nagauri, in Sagami, and inclosed some provisional regulations; but I have now
                    been informed by the authorities that it has been decided that vessels which,
                    upon being examined by the health officer, are found to have had no cases of
                    cholera during the voyage, will be allowed to enter port after the lapse of
                    seven days, calculated from the day on which they left the diseased port.</p>
                <p>I take, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>TERASHIMA MUNENORI</signed>, [<hi rendition="#small-caps">l.
                        s.</hi>]<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs</hi>.</closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency Sir <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry S. Parkes</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
